<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Slava: Help</title>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_head.html.erb' %>
    <meta name="description" content="How to use Slava: connect Strava, post activities in Slack, unfurl Strava links, view stats and leaderboards, and configure team settings."/>
    <meta property="og:title" content="Slava: Help">
    <meta property="og:description" content="How to use Slava: connect Strava, post activities in Slack, unfurl Strava links, view stats and leaderboards, and configure team settings.">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Slava: Help">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="How to use Slava: connect Strava, post activities in Slack, unfurl Strava links, view stats and leaderboards, and configure team settings.">
  </head>
  <body id="page-top" class="site-page help-page">
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_navigation.html.erb' %>
    <main id="main" class="page-container help-content">
      <header class="help-header">
        <h1>Slava: Help</h1>
        <p>Connect Strava, share activities, and manage your Slack channel.</p>
      </header>
      <section id="get-started" class="help-section">
        <h2>Get started</h2>
        <p>You'll need a Slack workspace and a Strava account. <a href="https://www.strava.com/register">Sign up for Strava</a> if you need one.</p>
        <ol class="getting-started-steps">
          <li><a href="https://slack.com/oauth/authorize?scope=<%= ENV['SLACK_OAUTH_SCOPE'] %>&client_id=<%= ENV['SLACK_CLIENT_ID'] %>">Add Slava to Slack</a> and authorize it for your workspace.</li>
          <li>Invite <code>@slava</code> to the channels where you want activities to appear.</li>
          <li>Use <code>/slava connect</code> or DM <code>connect</code> to <code>@slava</code>, then follow the link to authorize Strava.</li>
          <li>Save a new Strava activity. Notifications appear in channels where Slava is a member.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="help-note">To stop sharing, use <code>/slava disconnect</code> or DM <code>disconnect</code>.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="commands" class="help-section">
        <h2>Commands and settings</h2>
        <p>Use slash commands in Slack, or DM commands to @slava without the /slava prefix. Choose a topic for examples.</p>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Leaderboards and statistics</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>/slava leaderboard</code></dt>
            <dd>Show the channel's distance leaderboard. Choose a metric with <code>/slava leaderboard distance</code>, <code>/slava leaderboard time</code>, or <code>/slava leaderboard count</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/slava stats</code></dt>
            <dd>Show aggregate activity statistics for the past 30 days.</dd>
            <dt><code>/slava leaderboard last week</code></dt>
            <dd>Stats and leaderboards accept <code>weekly</code>, <code>monthly</code>, <code>quarterly</code>, or <code>yearly</code>, as well as date ranges such as <code>elapsed time last month</code>, <code>since 2024</code>, or <code>between January and March</code>. Longer ranges may require increasing retention below.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Sharing and privacy</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>set sync false</code></dt>
            <dd>Pause activity sharing. Resume with <code>set sync true</code> (the default).</dd>
            <dt><code>set private true</code></dt>
            <dd>Include private activities. They are hidden by default; restore that setting with <code>set private false</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>set followers false</code></dt>
            <dd>Hide followers-only activities. They are included by default; restore with <code>set followers true</code>.</dd>
            <dt><code>/slava disconnect</code></dt>
            <dd>Unlink your Strava account. This stops future activity sharing.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Units, maps, and fields</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>set units metric</code></dt>
            <dd>Use kilometers, meters, and Celsius. Choose <code>imperial</code> for miles, feet, yards, and Fahrenheit (the default), or <code>both</code> to display both sets.</dd>
            <dt><code>set maps thumb</code></dt>
            <dd>Use map thumbnails. Choose <code>off</code> to hide maps or <code>full</code> for full maps (the default).</dd>
            <dt><code>set fields</code></dt>
            <dd>Choose displayed fields with <code>default</code>, <code>all</code>, or <code>none</code>. Available fields: <%= ActivityFields.values.and { |v| '<code>' + v + '</code>' } %>.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
        <details class="help-topic">
          <summary>Retention, threading, and link previews</summary>
          <dl>
            <dt><code>set retention 60 days</code></dt>
            <dd>Change the default 30-day retention. Durations such as <code>6 months</code> also work.</dd>
            <dt><code>set threads daily</code></dt>
            <dd>Group activities into <code>daily</code>, <code>weekly</code>, or <code>monthly</code> threads. Use <code>activity</code> for a channel summary with details in a thread, or <code>none</code> to disable threading (the default).</dd>
            <dt><code>set leaderboard</code></dt>
            <dd>Configure the default leaderboard. DM <code>set</code> to see current settings.</dd>
            <dt>Strava link previews</dt>
            <dd>Paste a registered user's Strava activity link into Slack to unfurl it. DM <code>help</code> for more commands.</dd>
          </dl>
        </details>
      </section>
      <section id="support" class="help-section">
        <h2>Contact support</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:dblock@vestris.com">dblock@vestris.com</a> with the command, channel type, approximate time and time zone, and any error message. Don't send passwords or access tokens.</p>
      </section>
      <p class="affiliation-note">Powered by Strava; not officially affiliated with <a href="https://www.nyrr.org/">NYRR</a> or <a href="https://www.strava.com">Strava</a>.</p>
    </main>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_footer.html.erb' %>
  </body>
</html>
